      "hasMediaInOriginal": false,
      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "⚡⚽🇪🇺 All 55 UEFA member countries voted in favor of boycotting the World Cup if Gianni Infantino moves forward with the project to open a subsidiary company of FIFA to private investors.\nThe plan involves the creation of the FIFA Forward Enterprise (FEE), valued at $20 billion, with the sale of 20% of the shares to raise $4.2 billion by the end of the year. \n\nThe FFE will handle the sale of all rights connected to FIFA (sponsorships, tickets, licenses, television packages) and the operational management of tournaments. \n\nAmong the main investors is Thrive Eternal, a company led by Josh Kushner, the younger brother of Jared Kushner, son-in-law of Donald Trump.\n\n@medmannews",
